00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.900
If your eye muscles are active all day

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:07.090
and during your REM
cycle, when do they rest?

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:07.930
It's a cycle

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.480
so they're not constantly
going throughout the night.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.540
There are periods where
there's non-REM sleep

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.270
and your eye muscles are relaxed.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.440
Also, it's important to
note that different muscles

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.750
have different utilities

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.400
and some need more rest than others.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.940
Your cardiac muscle
almost never gets a break

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:24.010
during the short time that it relaxes,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.470
but your heart beats maybe a
hundred thousand times a day

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.460
on average.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.310
It's a lot of work,

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.140
