00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.840
Is there a difference between
CPR and chest compressions?

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:16.570
CPR just means
cardiopulmonary resuscitation.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:17.920
Chest compressions are part of that.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:20.040
We used to give rescue
breaths, but we realized

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.240
that there wasn't enough
benefit to doing so.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:23.230
It actually stopped people

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.880
from performing the chest compressions,

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.880
which are actually the
most important thing

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.460
to increase someone's
survivability until help arrives.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.510
Bronwyn S.

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:34.390
Is it safer to wear over-ear
or in-ear headphones?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.670
Oh, I'm very passionate about this.

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:38.920
First of all, if you are
cycling or running outside

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.330
and there are motor vehicles around,

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:43.280
make sure you do not use
noise-canceling headphones.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.650
It will save your life.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:48.770
Second, if you use in-ear
headphones and you have earwax,

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.950
the earwax gets pushed further
and further, further back,

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.190
and then it starts clogging your ears,

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:54.310
which can lead to you
developing an infection.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.030
When you're listening
with your headphones,

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.280
whether they're on-ear or in-ear
or over-the-ear headphones,

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:04.140
make sure that you're listening
to less than 60% volume,

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:06.480
because you will damage
your hearing over time

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.810
if you continue listening above 60%.

